# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy below is defence in depth, NOT the defence.
# guide-sanitise.js is what stops a hostile guide executing; this is the
# second line for the case where the sanitiser has a hole in it.
#
# ---- the honest limitation ----
# script-src carries 'unsafe-inline' because every page in this site keeps
# its logic in an inline <script> block. That is the single biggest thing
# weakening this policy: with 'unsafe-inline' present, CSP cannot stop
# injected script, which is the attack it exists to stop.
#
# Removing it means moving each page's inline script into its own .js file
# (or pinning every block with a sha256- hash, which breaks on every edit).
# That is a real piece of work and it is worth doing before this site takes
# guides from strangers. Until then the rest of the policy still earns its
# place: object-src and base-uri close off two injection routes that do not
# need script at all, and the src lists mean a successful injection still
# cannot reach a server that isn't listed here.
#
# connect-src names the Supabase project explicitly. Forget this and every
# API call is blocked with no visible error except the site appearing to
# have no guides at all — an hour of confusion for a one-line omission.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://ddragon.leagueoflegends.com https://raw.communitydragon.org; connect-src 'self' https://ddragon.leagueoflegends.com https://raw.communitydragon.org https://egbhtuhaatyclufktfla.supabase.co; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# The data files change when Riot patches, so they are checked often and
# cached briefly. The art never changes for a given URL.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, must-revalidate
/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, must-revalidate
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
